From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:14:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clutter/texture-content: Skip textures of a defunct context

After a graphics reset, a ClutterTextureContent can still hold a
texture from the context that was replaced until its owner provides a
new one. That texture's GL name is stale, and in the new context it can
name an unrelated texture, which was then painted in its place.

Paint nothing until the owner provides a texture from the new context.
---
 clutter/clutter/clutter-texture-content.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/clutter/clutter/clutter-texture-content.c b/clutter/clutter/clutter-texture-content.c
index 837e25564..4ba0cae0e 100644
--- a/clutter/clutter/clutter-texture-content.c
+++ b/clutter/clutter/clutter-texture-content.c
@@ -76,6 +76,9 @@ clutter_texture_content_paint_content (ClutterContent      *content,
   ClutterTextureContent *texture_content = CLUTTER_TEXTURE_CONTENT (content);
   ClutterPaintNode *node;
 
+  if (cogl_context_is_defunct (cogl_texture_get_context (texture_content->texture)))
+    return;
+
   node = clutter_actor_create_texture_paint_node (actor,
                                                   texture_content->texture);
   clutter_paint_node_set_static_name (node, "Texture Content");
